Fix the intermittent collect-news failures: anime_details.format enum mismatch

collect-news has failed 42 of its last 47 runs (hence the "All jobs have failed"
emails). The failing step is "Rebuild datasets", i.e. build_dataset.py exiting 1
on schema validation.

Cause: work.schema.json allowed anime_details.format ∈ {tv, movie, ova, web}
but collectors/anime.py emits eight formats — tv, movie, ova, ona, tv_short,
special, music, other. As soon as a run matched a work to an ONA or a special,
build_dataset.py wrote a value the schema rejects and the job went red. It is
intermittent because it depends on which works happen to match that run;
collect-news crawls 20 catalogue pages versus 6 in the daily job, so it matches
more anime and hits the bad values far more often.

This also explains why the last five runs "passed": the dataset had collapsed to
35 works, so nothing matched and the invalid value never appeared.

Fix:
* work.schema.json: widen the enum to the eight formats the collector can emit
  (drop the unused "web", which no data ever contained).
* web/lib/types.ts: widen AnimeFormat to match, with a note on why the two must
  move together; lib/anime-labels.ts already had labels for all eight.
* scripts/validate_schema.py: new cross-file assertion that the schema enum is a
  superset of every format actually present in data/anime.json. This is the check
  that would have caught the bug: the schema alone looks perfectly valid.
  Verified by reverting the enum — it then reports exactly
  [music, ona, other, special, tv_short].
